Z||000000||Hawkman||06-22-2000||09:10 AM||||I took my 85 4cyl in for a front end alignment and during the process the mechanic pointed out some problem signs under the car.  <P>He described that the motor mounts are soft and should be replaced.  After test driving the car he said that the engine jerks quite a bit and that the alignment problem could be caused by the engine torquing the suspension out of shape. He pushed a probe into mounts on either side of the oil pan to show me they were soft. I'm having an ongoing problem with the engine jerking (under light to no load) and I see the logic in his description.<P>And now the question...<BR>How many motor/tranny mounts are there on my 4 cylinder engine and were do they mount?  <P>I went to the parts store and they showed a total of four mounts in their computer.  One is the "wishbone" mount. I remember that one is visible from above.  Two were "transmission" mounts, and the last one a "motor" mount.  The parts guy had little clue how it all went together so I draw once again on the wisdom of you fine folks.<P>Help me ObeWan - you're my only hope!||||reg||5
Z||000001||lowCG||06-22-2000||10:35 AM||||While it's a good idea to have decent motor mounts,for many reasons,the suspension isn't going to be affected by this,and is an independant system.The axles will be turned while at some odd angles,but it stops there.<BR>I made the same assumption on a previous thread,and was corrected on that one.||||reg||1
